Amman hosted an emergency ministerial meeting on Wednesday to rally support behind Jordan’s custodianship of Jerusalem’s holy sites, as Foreign Minister Ayman Safadi warned that Israeli measures risk igniting a wider religious conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/20492c38-4fc7-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ISRAEL-JERUSALEM-MARCHE-DRAPEAUX-14MAI2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/20492c38-4fc7-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ISRAEL-JERUSALEM-MARCHE-DRAPEAUX-14MAI2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6d802474-90be-11f1-989c-6f8594e3bf55</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 15:07:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/20492c38-4fc7-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ISRAEL-JERUSALEM-MARCHE-DRAPEAUX-14MAI2026.jpg">AP Photo/Leo Correa - Leo Correa</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France announces further investment to combat drug trafficking in Guiana</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260805-france-announces-further-investment-to-combat-drug-trafficking-in-guiana</link><description>
France's Minister for Public Accounts outlined on Monday a slew of measures designed to combat drug trafficking in the Caribbean territory of French Guiana, one of the world's major hubs for smugglers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/207515aa-109f-11ea-8b9e-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1cs3o3_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/207515aa-109f-11ea-8b9e-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1cs3o3_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50a3dbf2-9005-11f1-953c-63f11d1765e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 08:54:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/207515aa-109f-11ea-8b9e-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1cs3o3_0.jpg">jody amiet / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Kremlin critic leaves Moscow for Paris after ban from running for election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260805-kremlin-critic-leaves-moscow-for-paris-after-ban-from-running-for-election</link><description>
Russian anti-war politician Boris Nadezhdin has left the country after being prevented from standing in September’s parliamentary elections, becoming the latest prominent Kremlin critic to move abroad amid an intensifying crackdown on dissent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f86556b0-8fe0-11f1-971f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2FB468.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f86556b0-8fe0-11f1-971f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2FB468.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f61fbd0-8fdd-11f1-80f1-75c61b62a88b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 06:06:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f86556b0-8fe0-11f1-971f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2FB468.jpg">AFP - ALEXANDER NEMENOV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Seventh round of talks between Lebanon and Israel under way in Rome</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260804-seventh-round-of-talks-between-lebanon-and-israel-under-way-in-rome</link><description>
Lebanon and Israel began a new round of United States-sponsored direct talks in Rome on Tuesday, as Beirut seeks Israel's phased withdrawal from the country's south. But critics, including Hezbollah, say the talks amount to a "surrender" by Lebanon. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/72f0f3a8-7f79-11f1-b507-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8W838U.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/72f0f3a8-7f79-11f1-b507-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8W838U.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb916a96-8ff6-11f1-ad54-9fd2dadcada1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 20:06:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/72f0f3a8-7f79-11f1-b507-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8W838U.jpg">AFP - JACK GUEZ</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU ministers agree Schengen zone 'not the problem' in Ceuta migrant influx</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260804-eu-ministers-agree-schengen-zone-not-the-problem-in-ceuta-migrant-influx</link><description>
Last week's deadly surge of migrants into Spain's North African enclave Ceuta did not "compromise" the European Union's visa-free Schengen travel zone, the Spanish interior minister said on Tuesday, following an emergency meeting at which member states affirmed their solidarity with Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/08d841ec-8f4b-11f1-bc9e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26214565552543.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/08d841ec-8f4b-11f1-bc9e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26214565552543.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">073db1d2-900e-11f1-900c-6b2982d35c03</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 15:23:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/08d841ec-8f4b-11f1-bc9e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26214565552543.jpg">AP Photo/Bernat Armangue - Bernat Armangue</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ceuta migrants caught between humanitarian disaster and diplomatic row</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260804-ceuta-migrants-caught-between-humanitarian-disaster-and-diplomatic-row</link><description>
While most of the estimated 50,000 migrants who arrived last week in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta have returned to Morocco, theories are circulating about what led to the mass arrival. RFI spoke to Spanish journalist Ignacio Cembrero, who specialises in migration between Spain and Morocco. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/085f5e8c-8d05-11f1-bee8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26212467836199.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/085f5e8c-8d05-11f1-bee8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26212467836199.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76b4a526-8fe0-11f1-8548-75c61b62a88b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 12:53:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/085f5e8c-8d05-11f1-bee8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26212467836199.jpg">AP Photo/Antonio Sempere - Antonio Sempere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Push for indictment as Lebanon marks six years since Beirut port blast</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260804-push-for-indictment-as-lebanon-marks-six-years-since-beirut-port-blast</link><description>
Lebanese President Joseph Aoun is urging the judiciary to issue a long-awaited indictment over the 2020 Beirut port blast, as the country marks six years since the catastrophe which killed more than 200 people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f99f4238-d6e2-11ea-a516-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/2020-08-05t052637z_876238970_rc2h7i9tqddc_rtrmadp_3_lebanon-security-blast_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f99f4238-d6e2-11ea-a516-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/2020-08-05t052637z_876238970_rc2h7i9tqddc_rtrmadp_3_lebanon-security-blast_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba5814ec-8f4b-11f1-9216-efe0ac09f616</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 05:46:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f99f4238-d6e2-11ea-a516-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/2020-08-05t052637z_876238970_rc2h7i9tqddc_rtrmadp_3_lebanon-security-blast_0.jpg">REUTERS/Mohamed Azakir</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU steps up AI regulation as new transparency rules come into effect</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260803-eu-steps-up-ai-regulation-as-new-transparency-rules-come-into-effect</link><description>
The European Union is stepping up its oversight of artificial intelligence this week, as the main provisions of its landmark AI Act become applicable, giving regulators stronger powers to inspect advanced models and sanction companies that break the rules.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5057dac8-8f3c-11f1-a171-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36RU8KY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5057dac8-8f3c-11f1-a171-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36RU8KY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d68ac5ba-8f0f-11f1-b557-fda0ec721e5e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 16:06:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5057dac8-8f3c-11f1-a171-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36RU8KY.jpg">AFP - KIRILL KUDRYAVTSEV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Deadly helicopter crash in Greece highlights danger to crews fighting wildfires</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260803-deadly-helicopter-crash-in-greece-exposes-growing-danger-of-europe-s-wildfires</link><description>
Water-bombing aircraft returned to the skies over Greece on Monday as firefighters battled several major blazes near Athens, a day after two pilots were killed when their fire-fighting helicopter collided with another aircraft.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7baa6236-8f2d-11f1-9e22-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RT8T6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7baa6236-8f2d-11f1-9e22-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RT8T6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">338b491a-8f10-11f1-b4a3-539eb0546072</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:16:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7baa6236-8f2d-11f1-9e22-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RT8T6.jpg">AFP - ANGELOS TZORTZINIS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU ministers to hold emergency meeting over migrant crossings to Ceuta</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260803-eu-ministers-set-to-meet-over-migrant-crossings-in-ceuta</link><description>
The European Union will hold an emergency video conference meeting of national ministers on Tuesday to discuss the mass migrant crossings into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4a8ffb0e-8f03-11f1-b586-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RV2BZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4a8ffb0e-8f03-11f1-b586-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RV2BZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e1f76250-8eab-11f1-b0dc-27f4398d8a9e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 06:16:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4a8ffb0e-8f03-11f1-b586-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RV2BZ.jpg">AFP - HENRY NICHOLLS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Why one American expert would be happy to see fewer US military bases in Europe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260802-why-one-american-expert-would-be-happy-to-see-fewer-us-military-bases-in-europe</link><description>
As Washington begins its review of the United States' military presence in Europe – confirmed this week by Under Secretary of War, Elbridge Colby – few observers welcome the prospect more than David Vine, a long-time critic of the sprawling network of American overseas bases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ad321b48-af66-11f0-b2e0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Allemagne-Etats-Unis-Ramstein.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ad321b48-af66-11f0-b2e0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Allemagne-Etats-Unis-Ramstein.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">404eb5d0-8c16-11f1-9756-1d72cbe21a0f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:11:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ad321b48-af66-11f0-b2e0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Allemagne-Etats-Unis-Ramstein.jpg">AFP - KIRILL KUDRYAVTSEV</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UN chief proposes fresh talks to Cyprus leaders, aiming to end 'frozen conflict'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260802-un-chief-proposes-fresh-talks-to-cyprus-leaders-aiming-to-end-frozen-conflict</link><description>
United Nations chief Antonio Guterres travelled to Cyprus this week with an offer of new peace talks – the latest attempt to resolve a conflict that has outlasted 11 of his predecessors. The island's division, sealed by Turkey's 1974 invasion but rooted in the flawed power-sharing constitution of 1960, is one of the world's longest-lasting frozen conflicts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33498b20-8b59-11f1-8972-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3FL36M.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33498b20-8b59-11f1-8972-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3FL36M.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e4ce246-8b59-11f1-a4b1-a54c6b50e563</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:12:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33498b20-8b59-11f1-8972-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3FL36M.jpg">AFP - PETROS KARADJIAS</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Fears of wheat price surge amid Ukraine-Russia clashes in the Black Sea</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260731-fears-of-wheat-price-surge-amid-ukraine-russia-clashes-in-the-black-sea</link><description>
Intensifying clashes between Ukraine and Russia in the Black Sea are threatening a crucial trade artery responsible for nearly a third of the world's wheat supply, stoking fears of soaring prices and shortages.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afa92442-844b-11f1-9ca2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200564414743.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afa92442-844b-11f1-9ca2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200564414743.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c468ccd0-8cdd-11f1-aaf0-0b9b6fc7e5a3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:20:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Anti-Semitic attacks at deadliest level in decades, global report warns</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260731-anti-semitic-attacks-at-deadliest-level-in-decades-global-report-warns</link><description>
Anti-Semitic violence reached its deadliest level in more than three decades last year, according to a report covering seven of the world’s largest Jewish communities outside Israel – with France recording a rise in physical assaults despite a decline in the overall number of incidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/34f25592-8b3b-11f1-a489-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36EX4YX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/34f25592-8b3b-11f1-a489-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36EX4YX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">959d6536-8b2b-11f1-909b-592ac6ceb892</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:51:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/34f25592-8b3b-11f1-a489-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36EX4YX.jpg">AFP - PASCAL GUYOT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>French national's spying conviction upheld by Azerbaijan court</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260731-french-national-s-spying-conviction-upheld-by-azerbaijan-court</link><description>
An Azerbaijani appeal court has upheld the 10-year sentence of a French national, Martin Ryan, for “espionage", in a case that arose against a backdrop of tensions between Paris and Baku. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d73f91e0-6f83-11f0-8755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP72253799240-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d73f91e0-6f83-11f0-8755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP72253799240-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9043fa1e-8bf3-11f1-8217-377d54a72fad</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:39:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d73f91e0-6f83-11f0-8755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP72253799240-1.jpg">AP - Luca Bruno</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>'Humanitarian emergency' as influx of migrants overwhelms Spanish enclave Ceuta</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260731-humanitarian-emergency-as-influx-of-migrants-overwhelms-spanish-enclave-ceuta</link><description>
Some 60,000 migrants entered Spain’s north African enclave of Ceuta from Morocco in the space of 24 hours, between Thursday and Friday, leaving at least 34 dead and prompting France to tighten controls along its border with Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8731f13c-8cb7-11f1-abbb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26211730761972.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8731f13c-8cb7-11f1-abbb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26211730761972.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2942eb1a-8cb9-11f1-aa04-51f91fa6bfb9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:20:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8731f13c-8cb7-11f1-abbb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26211730761972.jpg">AP Photo/Antonio Sempere - Antonio Sempere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Russia seeks arrest of Telegram's Durov over 'terrorism complicity' claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260730-russia-seeks-arrest-of-telegram-s-durov-over-terrorism-complicity-claims</link><description>
Russia has announced it is seeking the arrest of Telegram founder Pavel Durov over accusations of "complicity in terrorism", alleging he allowed the platform to be used for recruitment by Ukraine's security services.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/830ba85c-e3b9-11f0-a7a9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-79ZR2NE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/830ba85c-e3b9-11f0-a7a9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-79ZR2NE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e17ed11c-8bec-11f1-bd7a-8319c63ffefc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:34:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/830ba85c-e3b9-11f0-a7a9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-79ZR2NE.jpg">© AFP - GIUSEPPE CACACE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU crisis chief calls for prevention funding as wildfire crisis rages on</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260730-eu-crisis-chief-calls-for-prevention-funding-as-french-wildfire-crisis-rages-on</link><description>
As firefighters continue to battle major blazes in France, the European Union's crisis management chief is calling for more investment in prevention, forest management and emergency response.
